RIGHT-OF-WAY LICENSE AGREEMENT
This Right-of-Way License Agreement ("Agreement")is by and between the City of
Cheyenne, a municipal corporation organized and existing underthe laws of the State of Wyoming
("City"), whose address is 2101 O'Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming82001, and Volunteers of
America Northern Rockies("Licensee"), whose address is 1876S.Sheridan Avenue, Sheridan,
WY 82801.The City and the Licensee are collectively referred to as“Party”or“Parties."”This
Agreements hall become effective upon the date of the last signature affixed here to.
RECITALS:
WHEREAS, the Licensee holds title to and has developed approximately1.70 acres of land
in the City of Cheyenne, County of Laramie, State of Wyoming("Property”), more particularly
described as being:
Lot 1, Block 1, VOANR Cheyenne East, City of Cheyenne, Laramie County,
Wyoming;
and
WHEREAS, the Property is served by an exclusive underground drainage facility which
encroaches into the public right-of-way as shown on Exhibit A, attached hereto and incorporated
byreference("Facility"); and
WHEREAS, the City is prepared to grant a license to use a utility right-of-way(License"),
provided the Licensee agreesto certain terms and conditions.
NOW, THEREFORE, based on good and valuable consideration, the receipt and
sufficiency of which is hereby acknowledged, the Parties agree as follows:
1.
Grant of License.The City grants to Licensee, its successors and assigns, the
temporary, non-exclusive privilege of using the City right-of-way, commonly referred to as
Seymour Avenue covering a portion of thelands described as Township14North, Range66West
of the 6"h P.M., Laramie County, Wyoming, NE1/4 NE1/4 of Section 31, for a distance of
approximately1.6feet, to be used as a detention ondoutlet conveyance pipe, specifically subject
to the remaining terms and conditions set forth here in.The Licensee hereby accepts this License,
subject to the terms and conditions contained herein, and subject to any requirements or limitations
of law, now or in the future, which may restrict the use or enjoyment of this License.
2.Term; Termination.This Agreement shall not be effective until it is approved by
the Parties.This Agreement is a covenant running with the Property.Upon thirty(30) days written
notice, the Citymay terminate this Agreement and revoke the License granted hereby.Nothing in
this Agreement, nor the act of entering into this Agreement, shall be construed as a limitation of
the City's authority tomodify or abandon theright-of-way the City now has.
3. Responsibilities of Licensee. The Licensee, its successors and assigns, covenant
and agree toperform and abidebyeach andevery of the following:
